# Data conversion between gigabyte and terabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between gigabyte and terabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1GB to 0.001TB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5GB yields 0.0015TB; backward, converting 1TB to 1000GB preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5TB yields 1500.0GB.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1GB
print(forward_whole->to(TB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5GB
print(forward_fractional->to(TB))
backward_whole: int = 1TB
print(backward_whole->to(GB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TB
print(backward_fractional->to(GB))

<<< stdout
0.001TB
0.0015TB
1000GB
1500.0GB

<<< stderr
